{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 34,
  "title": "The legend of Vishvamitra's ancestry",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga34/balasans34.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga34/balaitrans34.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Vishvamitra narrates about the birth of Gaadhi, his own father and the son of Kushanaabha. Incidentally he narrates about the emergence and prominence of River Kaushiki, who is Vishwamitra's elder sister turned out as a sacred River."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे चतुस्त्रिंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 34th chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.34.1",
      "label": "1.34.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "कृतोद्वाहे गते तस्मिन् ब्रह्मदत्ते च राघव |\nअपुत्रः पुत्रलाभाय पौत्रीमिष्टिमकल्पयत्",
      "iast": "kṛta udvāhe gate tasmin brahmadatte ca rāghava |\naputraḥ putra lābhāya pautrīm iṣṭim akalpayat",
      "translation": "When Brahmadatta has married and left, oh, Raghava, king Kushanaabha he embarked on Vedic-ritual called putra kaameSTHi in order to beget a son because is sonless.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raaghava",
          "iast": "rāghava",
          "devanagari": "राघव",
          "meaning": "oh, Raghava",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tasmin brahmadatte",
          "iast": "tasmin brahmadatte",
          "devanagari": "तस्मिन् ब्रह्मदत्ते",
          "meaning": "of that, Brahmadatta's",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kR^ita udvaahe gate",
          "iast": "kṛta udvāhe gate",
          "devanagari": "कृत उद्वाहे गते",
          "meaning": "on making, marriage [on marrying,] when gone away",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "a putraH",
          "iast": "a putraḥ",
          "devanagari": "अ पुत्रः",
          "meaning": "not, with son - sonless",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "putra laabhaaya",
          "iast": "putra lābhāya",
          "devanagari": "पुत्र लाभाय",
          "meaning": "son, for achieving",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pautriim iSTim akalpayat",
          "iast": "pautrīm iṣṭim akalpayat",
          "devanagari": "पौत्रीं इष्टिं अकल्पयत्",
          "meaning": "for son's, ritual, embarked on.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.34.2",
      "label": "1.34.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "इष्ट्यां तु वर्तमानायां कुशनाभं महीपतिम् |\nउवाच परमोदारः कुशो ब्रह्मसुतस्तदा",
      "iast": "iṣṭyām tu vartamānāyām kuśanābham mahīpatim |\nuvāca paramodāraḥ kuśo brahmasutaḥ tadā",
      "translation": "During the performance of the ritual, supremely generous Kusha, the brainchild of Brahma and the father of Kushanaabha, spoke to the king Kushanaabha.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tadaa",
          "iast": "tadā",
          "devanagari": "तदा",
          "meaning": "then",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "iSTyaam tu vartamaanaayaam",
          "iast": "iṣṭyām tu vartamānāyām",
          "devanagari": "इष्ट्यां तु वर्तमानायां",
          "meaning": "ritual, but, while being conducted - during its performance",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "parama udaaraH",
          "iast": "parama udāraḥ",
          "devanagari": "परम उदारः",
          "meaning": "supremely, generous one",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "brahma sutaH kushaH",
          "iast": "brahma sutaḥ kuśaḥ",
          "devanagari": "ब्रह्म सुतः कुशः",
          "meaning": "Brahma's, brainchild, namely - Kusha",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kushanaabham mahiipatim uvaaca",
          "iast": "kuśanābham mahīpatim uvāca",
          "devanagari": "कुशनाभं महीपतिं उवाच",
          "meaning": "to Kushanaabha, king, spoke.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.34.3",
      "label": "1.34.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "पुत्र ते सदृशः पुत्रो भविष्यति सुधार्मिकः |\nगाधिं प्राप्स्यसि तेन त्वं कीर्तिं लोके च शाश्वतीम्",
      "iast": "putraḥ te sadṛśaḥ putra bhaviṣyati sudhārmikaḥ |\ngādhim prāpsyasi tena tvam kīrtim loke ca śāśvatīm",
      "translation": "\" 'Oh, son, there will be a highly virtuous and selfsame son of yours, known as Gaadhi, and through him you also will get everlasting renown in the world.' \" Thus Kusha said to Kushanaabha.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "putraH",
          "iast": "putraḥ",
          "devanagari": "पुत्रः",
          "meaning": "oh, son",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "te sadR^ishaH su dhaarmikaH putra",
          "iast": "te sadṛśaḥ su dhārmikaḥ putra",
          "devanagari": "ते सदृशः सु धार्मिकः पुत्र",
          "meaning": "to you, selfsame, highly, virtuous, son",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhaviSyati",
          "iast": "bhaviṣyati",
          "devanagari": "भविष्यति",
          "meaning": "will be there",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "gaadhim praapsyasi",
          "iast": "gādhim prāpsyasi",
          "devanagari": "गाधिं प्राप्स्यसि",
          "meaning": "Gadhi, you will get",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tena tvam loke shaashvatiim kiirtim ca",
          "iast": "tena tvam loke śāśvatīm kīrtim ca",
          "devanagari": "तेन त्वं लोके शाश्वतीं कीर्तिं च",
          "meaning": "by him, you, in world, everlasting, renown",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "[praapyasi",
          "iast": "[prāpyasi",
          "devanagari": "[प्राप्यसि",
          "meaning": "you will get.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
