        {
          "itrans": "parama dharmiSThaH",
          "iast": "parama dharmiṣṭhaḥ",
          "devanagari": "परम धर्मिष्ठः",
          "meaning": "supremely, righteous one",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "naamataH gaadhiH iti eva",
          "iast": "nāmataḥ gādhiḥ iti eva",
          "devanagari": "नामतः गाधिः इति एव",
          "meaning": "by name, Gaadhi, thus, [known] as",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "jaj~ne",
          "iast": "jajñe",
          "devanagari": "जज्ञे",
          "meaning": "took birth.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.34.6",
      "label": "1.34.6",
      "numbers": [
        6
      ],
      "devanagari": "स पिता मम काकुत्स्थ गाधिः परमधार्मिकः |\nकुशवंशप्रसूतोऽस्मि कौशिको रघुनंदन",
      "iast": "sa pitā mama kākutstha gādhiḥ parama dhārmikaḥ |\nkuśa vaṃśa prasūto asmi kauśiko raghunandana",
      "translation": "\"Oh, Rama of Kakutstha dynasty, that eminently righteous Gaadhi is my father, and since I am born in Kusha dynasty, oh, Raghu's legatee, I got the name Kaushika.\" Sage Vishvamitra thus narrating to Rama.",
